        "agentId": "reed",
        "decision": "reject",
        "reason": "Grassland roots or basal shoots are physically plausible, but terrain at (35,7) is not an existing forage site and has no established harvestable stock. Ecological rules allocate resources only to matching existing natural sites; they cannot create a patch at a requested coordinate. Adding a plant type would not create an instance or establish its presence here. Direct consumption also requires an owned food stack, not bare terrain. No supported local target instance, available stock, or direct-feeding ability can therefore be supplied.",
        "prerequisites": [
          "An actual accessible natural forage site with finite matching plant stock, or an accessible food stack.",
          "Establish the unfamiliar plant's properties before relying on it as safe food.",
          "Gather site stock into owned inventory before consuming it with the existing eating ability."
        ],
        "learningRounds": 0,
        "mechanicId": null
      }
    ]
  }
}

{
  "needsDevelopment": true,
  "proposal": {
    "resources": [],
    "ecology": [],
    "mechanics": [],
    "reviews": [
      {
        "agentId": "lin",
        "decision": "reject",
        "reason": "Direct browsing is physically plausible and would require one learning round, but the current operation format cannot implement this single-tree-target request. Extraction creates an owned stack, while consumption requires an owned stack ID; no operation can bind the newly extracted portion for consumption within the same transaction. A transactional output reference or finite-site consumption operation must be resolved before acceptance. This implementation issue does not advance game time or replenish foliage.",
        "prerequisites": [
          "Resolve transactional consumption of the newly extracted portion without requiring a separate action or a pre-existing inventory stack.",
          "An adjacent tree must already contain a reachable portion of suitable nutritious foliage; leafy appearance alone is insufficient.",
          "Existing ecological allocations remain unchanged, including empty or exhausted allocations.",
          "No tools or additional materials are required; consumption must apply actual food properties and the normal satiety cap without healing."
        ],
        "learningRounds": 0,
        "mechanicId": null
      }
    ]
  }
}

{
  "needsDevelopment": true,
  "proposal": {
    "resources": [],
    "ecology": [],
    "mechanics": [],
    "reviews": [
      {
        "agentId": "lin",
        "decision": "reject",
        "reason": "Direct browsing is physically plausible, but cannot yet be registered as executable: consume accepts only an owned stack, and extract cannot pass its output to a later operation. A concrete engine extension is required for atomic finite-site consumption: validate adjacency and existing matching nutritious stock, subtract one portion, and apply that type's actual nutrition and toxicity under normal satiety and transaction rules. It must not allocate or replenish stock, infer safety from appearance, or change survival settlement order. Development does not advance game time. Once supported, this simple browsing technique warrants one learning round; availability at the requested tree remains unverified.",
        "prerequisites": [
          "Engine support for atomic finite-site consumption or transactional extraction-output references",
          "An adjacent natural site with an existing reachable portion of matching nutritious foliage",
          "Prior verification of foliage properties and remaining stock for the requested safe-food condition",
          "No tools or additional materials"
        ],
        "learningRounds": 0,
        "mechanicId": null
      }
    ]
  }
}

